<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<dtmd:DecisionTaskMetaData xmlns:stc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/SSPTraceabilityCommon" xmlns:dtmd="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/DecisionTaskMetaData" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:ssc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSP1/SystemStructureCommon" version="1.0.0" name="InfiniRange Gate 2 Range Substantiation Decision" GUID="97510c82-3603-40df-9022-5f75510983cb" generationTool="LOTAR 2026 worked example (Claude)" generationDateAndTime="2026-08-07T00:00:00Z">
  <dtmd:GeneralInformation><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_gi1"><stc:Content>Decision task governing the InfiniRange Gate 2 range/efficiency substantiation for torque-arbitration control strategy and battery-variant selection. Commissions the range-sensitivity SimulationTaskMetaData and the two ModelingTaskMetaData records for EVExample.FMUs.Intermediate.ElectricRange_V2 and EVExample.FMUs.TorqueArbitration.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></dtmd:GeneralInformation>
  <dtmd:AnalysisPhase>
    <dtmd:AnalyzeDecisionTask><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_an_in1"><stc:Content>InfiniRange Powertrain Development Gate 2 milestone charter: a range/efficiency substantiation package is required before the torque-arbitration control strategy and battery-variant lineup can be released for tooling commitment.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_an_proc1"><stc:Content>Applied the Vehicle Programs Simulation Governance Board's decision-task framing checklist: identify the engineering question, the decision it feeds, and the financial/technical materiality of getting it wrong, per the company's Simulation Governance Charter (Rev. 4).</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_an_out1"><stc:Content>Decision-task charter: commission a dedicated range-sensitivity simulation task covering WLTP and NEDC drive cycles, aggressive vs. standard regenerative-brake blending, and four battery-capacity variants, to substantiate the Gate 2 tooling release decision for torque arbitration control logic and battery sizing.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_an_rat1"><stc:Content>Gate 2 tooling commitment is financially material (asymmetric downside if regen blending under-delivers post-tooling) and technically novel (more aggressive generative-braking use than the predecessor platform), so an explicit, documented decision task is warranted rather than an informal engineering request.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-02T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Programs" role="Decision Maker" name="R. Halvorsen"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:AnalyzeDecisionTask>
  <dtmd:VerifyAnalysis><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifyAnalysis-Input.md"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifyAnalysis-Procedure.md"/></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifyAnalysis-Output.md"/></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifyAnalysis-Rationale.md"/></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Drafted date="2026-09-05T00:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="Fixture Authoring" role="Simulation Engineer" name="Fixture Generator"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Drafted></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:VerifyAnalysis></dtmd:AnalysisPhase>
  <dtmd:DefinitionPhase>
    <dtmd:DefineSubTasks><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dt_an_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ds_proc1"><stc:Content>Decomposed the charter into one Credible Simulation Process task and two Credible Modelling Process tasks, scoping model-level records to the two models under active change for this decision; the drive-cycle and ambient sub-models are reused unchanged from a prior, already-credentialed release and do not need a fresh modelling record.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ds_out1"><stc:Content>Sub-tasks defined: (1) SimulationTaskMetaData 'ArchitectureLevelRange' -- WLTP/NEDC range-sensitivity task, packaged at extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.stmd/ SimulationTask.stmd; (2) ModelingTaskMetaData for EVExample.FMUs.Intermediate.ElectricRange_V2, packaged at extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.mtmd/ElectricRange_V2.mtmd; (3) ModelingTaskMetaData for EVExample.FMUs.TorqueArbitration, packaged at extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.mtmd/TorqueControl.mtmd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ds_rat1"><stc:Content>Splitting the range model and the torque-arbitration controller into separate modelling tasks matches their separate ownership (vehicle energy systems CAE vs. controls) and separate change cadence, and mirrors the existing SRMD/STMD scope, which already treats them as the two models under credibility assessment.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-04T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Programs" role="Decision Maker" name="R. Halvorsen"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:DefineSubTasks>
    <dtmd:DefineResultQuality id="sig-e44470f0b3b3"><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dt_an_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet" id="id_dt_drq_proc1" description="Company Simulation Risk Assessment Matrix (financial materiality x technical novelty x decision reversibility), completed for this decision task."><stc:Content>Company Simulation Risk Assessment Matrix, InfiniRange Gate 2 range/efficiency decision -- scores recorded in this step's Procedure text.</stc:Content></stc:Resource><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_drq_proc2"><stc:Content>Scored: financial materiality = High (tooling commitment, asymmetric downside); technical novelty = Medium-High (aggressive regen blending is a meaningful departure from the predecessor control strategy, but uses previously validated component models); decision reversibility = Medium (a software recalibration, not a hardware re-spin, can correct a wrong call pre-production).</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_drq_out1" description="Assigned LOTAR risk level for this decision task's sub-tasks."><stc:Content>Assigned risk level R3 (High) for both spawned sub-tasks.</stc:Content></stc:Resource><stc:Classification type="org.credible-process.core" xlink:type="simple"><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="credibility.level" xlink:type="simple">CL3</stc:ClassificationEntry></stc:Classification></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_drq_rat1"><stc:Content>R3 rather than R4: failure modes are recoverable pre-production and the underlying component models (motor, converter, battery) are reused, already-validated library content -- only the regen-blending control strategy and its resulting range claim are novel. R3 rather than R2: the Gate 2 tooling decision is financially material and the control strategy has not been exercised on this vehicle platform before.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-05T14:30:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Programs" role="Decision Maker" name="R. Halvorsen"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"><ssc:Content><ds:Signature xmlns:ds="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#" xmlns:xades="http://uri.etsi.org/01903/v1.3.2#" Id="SignXMLSignatureC5ECA049"><ds:SignedInfo><ds:CanonicalizationMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/xml-c14n11"/><ds:SignatureMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmldsig-more#rsa-sha256"/><ds:Reference URI="#sig-e44470f0b3b3" Id="SignXMLReferenceFE6BC15D"><ds:Transforms><ds:Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#enveloped-signature"/><ds:Transform Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/xml-c14n11"/></ds:Transforms><ds:DigestMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#sha256"/><ds:DigestValue>qrZuHVhP8aax8hBF5Af6EA3JwvHbIXW2ZphyXAAUg8s=</ds:DigestValue></ds:Reference><ds:Reference URI="#SignXMLSignatureC5ECA049-SignedProperties5B06E397" Type="http://uri.etsi.org/01903#SignedProperties"><ds:DigestMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#sha256"/><ds:DigestValue>pZE7hmMGom6/k+Hnr8mUZbIvIPzfEFgBkysp1BjXofE=</ds:DigestValue></ds:Reference><ds:Reference URI="#SignXMLCertificate0885E738"><ds:DigestMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#sha256"/><ds:DigestValue>P6hcXiUdioAvJpI1YE/spYSx6cwFG02HBYkfAjrdyKY=</ds:DigestValue></ds:Reference></ds:SignedInfo><ds:SignatureValue></ds:SignatureValue><ds:KeyInfo Id="SignXMLCertificate0885E738"><ds:KeyValue><ds:RSAKeyValue><ds:Modulus></ds:Modulus><ds:Exponent>AQAB</ds:Exponent></ds:RSAKeyValue></ds:KeyValue><ds:X509Data><ds:X509Certificate>MIIDKTCCAhGgAwIBAgIUeAYFJND31ZOvuD13/MrJzCRH+UAwDQYJKoZIhvcNAQEL
