  <dtmd:VerifySubTasks><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifySubTasks-Input.md"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifySubTasks-Procedure.md"/></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifySubTasks-Output.md"/></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/VerifySubTasks-Rationale.md"/></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Drafted date="2026-09-05T00:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="Fixture Authoring" role="Simulation Engineer" name="Fixture Generator"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Drafted></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:VerifySubTasks></dtmd:DefinitionPhase>
  <dtmd:ExecutionPhase>
    <dtmd:PerformSubTasks><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dt_ds_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ps_proc1"><stc:Content>Execution and quality assurance of each sub-task is delegated to, and recorded within, its own STMD/MTMD process record; this step tracks only that all three sub-tasks reached a signed-off life-cycle state, per LOTAR's separation between the decision record and the technical process records it commissions.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ps_out1"><stc:Content>Confirmed: SimulationTask.stmd, ElectricRange_V2.mtmd and TorqueControl.mtmd all reached an Approved life-cycle state at their respective DecideSimulationObjectiveFulfillment / DecideModelingObjectiveFulfillment steps.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_ps_rat1"><stc:Content>Tracking completion status here (rather than re-deriving it) avoids duplicating process detail that already has a single source of truth in the sub-task records themselves.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-30T16:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:PerformSubTasks>
  </dtmd:ExecutionPhase>
  <dtmd:EvaluationPhase>
    <dtmd:EvaluateResults><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dt_ps_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_er_proc1"><stc:Content>Reviewed the STMD's EvaluateSimulationResults and AssureSimulationQuality outputs (WLTP/NEDC range deltas across the four battery variants and two regen-blending strategies) against the Gate 2 acceptance threshold of a minimum +4% combined-cycle range improvement from more aggressive regenerative braking.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_er_out1"><stc:Content>More aggressive regen blending shows a credible +5.1% to +6.8% combined-cycle range improvement across battery variants, above the +4% acceptance threshold, with uncertainty bounds from the model's own validation/UQ record. Standard and Extended battery variants both clear the threshold; ExtendedPlus was not part of this task's scope.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_er_rat1"><stc:Content>Directly answers the original question of interest recorded in the SRMD (cred-assessment-sim.question-of-interest): quantifying the range gain achievable through more aggressive brake blending.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-08-01T10:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:EvaluateResults>
  <dtmd:AssureResultQuality><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/AssureResultQuality-Input.md"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/AssureResultQuality-Procedure.md"/></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/AssureResultQuality-Output.md"/></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/AssureResultQuality-Rationale.md"/></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Drafted date="2026-09-05T00:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="Fixture Authoring" role="Simulation Engineer" name="Fixture Generator"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Drafted></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:AssureResultQuality><dtmd:DeriveResultQualityVerdict><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/DeriveResultQualityVerdict-Input.md"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/DeriveResultQualityVerdict-Procedure.md"/></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/DeriveResultQualityVerdict-Output.md"/></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" source="resources/DeriveResultQualityVerdict-Rationale.md"/></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Drafted date="2026-09-05T00:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="Fixture Authoring" role="Simulation Engineer" name="Fixture Generator"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Drafted></stc:LifeCycleInformation></dtmd:DeriveResultQualityVerdict></dtmd:EvaluationPhase>
  <dtmd:FulfillmentPhase>
    <dtmd:DecideObjectiveFulfillment id="sig-f1a950c5a619"><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_dt_er_out1"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_do_proc1"><stc:Content>Decision Maker review of the evaluation summary against the objective set in AnalyzeDecisionTask, per the Simulation Governance Charter's Gate 2 sign-off procedure.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_do_out1"><stc:Content>Objective fulfilled. Approved advancing the more aggressive regenerative-brake blending strategy ('AgressiveRegeneration' controller parameter variant) together with the Standard battery variant to Gate 2 tooling release, contingent on a production-code review of the released torque-arbitration controller logic against this task's calibration.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_dt_do_rat1"><stc:Content>Range-gain evidence clears the Gate 2 threshold with margin; residual risk (control strategy is novel to this platform) is judged acceptable at the assigned R3 level, consistent with DefineResultQuality's rationale, and is retired by the production-code-review contingency rather than by further simulation.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-08-04T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Programs" role="Decision Maker" name="R. Halvorsen"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"><ssc:Content><ds:Signature xmlns:ds="http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#" xmlns:xades="http://uri.etsi.org/01903/v1.3.2#" Id="SignXMLSignature418E92F2"><ds:SignedInfo><ds:CanonicalizationMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/xml-c14n11"/><ds:SignatureMethod Algorithm="http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmldsig-more#rsa-sha256"/><ds:Reference URI="#sig-f1a950c5a619" Id="SignXMLReference2D2A028C"><ds: